maluos-memory (0.1.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * ask_self: an own identity is asked at this face's own listener. The
    directory publishes a desk at the overlay address the office allocated to
    the desk's key, which a desktop that is also a node never carries (its
    interface is the node's): the one-host proof got "connection refused".

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 03:10:00 +0000

maluos-memory (0.1.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * fanout_s defaults to 5 s (2 s was tight for two parallel queries at an
    emulated CPU, and for a slow holder on a real estate); memory.yaml sets it.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 00:10:00 +0000

maluos-memory (0.1.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The face never asks, or replicates from, this host's own identities (a desk that is
    a node too is published itself through the other membership); memory.yaml `ask_self:
    true` keeps the one-host proofs.
    A write above the writer's ceiling (the facade's check option) is refused 403
    classification instead of an internal error.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:50:00 +0000

maluos-memory (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 13 slice 4 (docs/phase13-slice4-memory.md): the memory face of a
    MaluOS host. A Unix socket for local principals (recall, remember,
    forget, usage, the facts the heartbeat carries) and an overlay listener
    for the estate (a slice 2 envelope as the credential, verified against
    the peers the office publishes; the delegated scopes intersected with
    what this host shares; claims, never records). `maluctl memory`: status,
    facts, whoami, recall [--estate], remember, forget, usage, share,
    unshare, expose, unexpose, keys, sync, reload. The first-boot component
    makes the role, the guest and sync principals and the configuration.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000
